                "word": "poufiasse",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "93f844eb-a5c2-4724-96fb-f858653c8c1e",
                        "entry_id": "30bc404b-77f2-32b7-ac95-2967ac6810d2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "poufiasses"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "3efa5021-a964-40ba-8c01-47866288fa4e",
                        "entry_id": "30bc404b-77f2-32b7-ac95-2967ac6810d2",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "pouffiasse"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "450a82a0-edf7-3f35-b70c-1a71715214f8",
                        "entry_id": "30bc404b-77f2-32b7-ac95-2967ac6810d2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Prostituée. ^([1])"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "offensive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5507df05-ba0d-4dd3-b66f-ca34996ec4e2",
                                "sense_id": "450a82a0-edf7-3f35-b70c-1a71715214f8",
                                "text": "Les privés de sortie les contemplaient, ces veinards, d’un œil mélancolique, quémandaient des impressions, un récit d’exploit. Ou bien, pour se consoler, rôdaient près de la porte Sainte-Claire qui donnait sur une ruelle obscure. Là, de jeunes poufiasses accouraient mendier des vivres, des mégots, en échange d’une caresse bâclée par l’entrebâillement des battants vermoulus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff30802d-e57b-4270-9428-4b37dd753660",
                                "sense_id": "450a82a0-edf7-3f35-b70c-1a71715214f8",
                                "text": "Les vierges du 16ᵉ venaient s’y donner des airs de pouffiasses de port de mer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9eb5f112-2d3e-4570-91ba-fb72be88eb15",
                                "sense_id": "450a82a0-edf7-3f35-b70c-1a71715214f8",
                                "text": "L’univers féerique que baigne la musique et que grignote çà et là le rire langoureux de quelques poufiasses éméchées, les superbes bagnoles vautrées dans le parc semblables aux vaches sacrées, le faste et l’incommensurable fatuité des grosses légumes, la lune pleine dans le ciel azuré, le froufrou béatifiant des fortunes, tout en cet endroit me fait vomir."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3909bd5a-8023-4232-811a-9fdb94bafc8b",
                                "sense_id": "450a82a0-edf7-3f35-b70c-1a71715214f8",
                                "text": "Car, bien entendu, pour une femme mariée, toute fille qui ose trouver son mari à son goût est une putain, une poufiasse, une ordure, une salope..."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4981d5a0-ea9d-3d6f-8a34-9f1d5f7793f5",
                        "entry_id": "30bc404b-77f2-32b7-ac95-2967ac6810d2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Femme grosse, laide et vulgaire. ^([1])"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "offensive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "88466a8b-2590-42ff-8313-03db85357662",
                                "sense_id": "4981d5a0-ea9d-3d6f-8a34-9f1d5f7793f5",
                                "text": "… elle eut en outre la douleur presque aussi grande de s’entendre appeler carcasse, macaque, poufiasse, autruche, momie, vadrouille et guenon."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c4a3f96-ad98-4584-bd30-da37c9940708",
                                "sense_id": "4981d5a0-ea9d-3d6f-8a34-9f1d5f7793f5",
                                "text": "Elles parlaient dans l'allée et se rangèrent pour laisser une dame du pays, qui s'exclama à voix très haute, en arrivant à la caisse, la grosse poufiasse, elle prend toute la place avec son bâtard dans les bras."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6c205d94-ccbc-425c-9662-d20773d96f6a",
                        "source_entry_id": "30bc404b-77f2-32b7-ac95-2967ac6810d2",
                        "target_lang_word": "tramp",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tramp",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1dfe2829-5724-3d92-84e8-2af53ef16bb4",
                                        "entry_id": "90bb58cd-46f3-3c13-af24-46162a335731",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A homeless person; a vagabond."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c489dae-d56f-4e25-a93f-9cf51441a1af",
                                                "sense_id": "1dfe2829-5724-3d92-84e8-2af53ef16bb4",
                                                "text": "[S]he had expected to discover a burglar of one or another accepted type—either a dashing cracksman in full-blown evening dress, lithe, polished, pantherish, or a common yegg, a red-eyed, unshaven, burly brute in the rags and tatters of a tramp."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8aacfd08-c298-33db-931f-010cd9eebb3a",
                                        "entry_id": "90bb58cd-46f3-3c13-af24-46162a335731",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A disreputable, promiscuous woman; a slut."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57ab1c6e-2a14-4599-a8f9-1eba5e44ffed",
                                                "sense_id": "8aacfd08-c298-33db-931f-010cd9eebb3a",
                                                "text": "I can't believe you'd let yourself be seen with that tramp."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1fc17d2-f94c-4b57-bc1f-13ada71a38b3",
                                                "sense_id": "8aacfd08-c298-33db-931f-010cd9eebb3a",
                                                "text": "Claudia is such a tramp; making out with all those men when she has a boyfriend."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "588053db-7b8d-3866-ad03-d20ed7e4d0fd",
                                        "entry_id": "90bb58cd-46f3-3c13-af24-46162a335731",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any ship which does not have a fixed schedule or published ports of call."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38bbadf2-1ef0-47cc-9670-3405e2d814d9",
                                                "sense_id": "588053db-7b8d-3866-ad03-d20ed7e4d0fd",
                                                "text": "I was so happy on board that ship, I could not have believed it possible. We had the beastliest weather, and many discomforts; but the mere fact of its being a tramp-ship gave us many comforts; we could cut about with the men and officers, stay in the wheel-house, discuss all manner of things, and really be a little at sea."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5b129c7-d827-4d51-a5d9-5226e7f51fc7",
                                                "sense_id": "588053db-7b8d-3866-ad03-d20ed7e4d0fd",
                                                "text": "Then I think I conceive of other worlds and vast structures that pass us by, within a few miles, without the slightest desire to communicate, quite as tramp vessels pass many islands without particularizing one from another."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e27adf41-3469-41a5-9e58-e63e24684751",
                                                "sense_id": "588053db-7b8d-3866-ad03-d20ed7e4d0fd",
                                                "text": "Some of these are regular ocean liners; others are casual tramp ships."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14f8d873-75ff-4250-aa2f-6a21d5cbec87",
                                                "sense_id": "588053db-7b8d-3866-ad03-d20ed7e4d0fd",
                                                "text": "Shipping of every sort, from passenger liners to ferry steamers, tramps to tugs and trailing barges, feluccas to speedboats and yachts, from warships to caiques, chugs, hoots, glides or churns its way in all directions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5911387d-d496-44f6-845a-81c7b2336e51",
                                                "sense_id": "588053db-7b8d-3866-ad03-d20ed7e4d0fd",
                                                "text": "“Hrrumph,” said the Mate. “Get into uniform right away, we must have discipline here.” With that he stalked off as if he were First Mate on one of the Queens instead of just on a dirty, rusty old tramp ship."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b9f1e8f-38f3-3c92-b6c0-2f1c043428b9",
                                        "entry_id": "90bb58cd-46f3-3c13-af24-46162a335731",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A long walk, possibly of more than one day, in a scenic or wilderness area."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "New-Zealand"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e980a3eb-1815-46bf-8673-63ce3da3eb89",
                                                "sense_id": "7b9f1e8f-38f3-3c92-b6c0-2f1c043428b9",
                                                "text": "I got in with the American Fur Company and set out for another tramp to trade with the Indians on the North and South Platte Rivers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6fb7d6d-109e-46c9-99e9-1397d2490ed8",
                                                "sense_id": "7b9f1e8f-38f3-3c92-b6c0-2f1c043428b9",
                                                "text": "The starting place for the tramp is reached over a gravel road that begins on Route 3 about a mile south of Gorham spur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3632e4e-cf15-4878-b0f9-c1c0431659c8",
                                                "sense_id": "7b9f1e8f-38f3-3c92-b6c0-2f1c043428b9",
                                                "text": "Speaking of knockout panoramas, if you′re fit then consider doing the taxing, winding, 8km tramp up Mt Roy (1578m; five to six hours return), start 6km from Wanaka on Mt Aspiring Rd."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fad475e-b80d-4656-9464-66fed01be279",
                                                "sense_id": "7b9f1e8f-38f3-3c92-b6c0-2f1c043428b9",
                                                "text": "The 1½-hour tramp passes through banksia, gum, and wattle forests, with spectacular views of peaks and valleys."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e69eb97-5a55-3db9-861e-1d875d1b8715",
                                        "entry_id": "90bb58cd-46f3-3c13-af24-46162a335731",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of objects, stray, intrusive and unwanted."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in apposition"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bd2fa6f-d349-4484-be06-351033f84a06",
                                                "sense_id": "9e69eb97-5a55-3db9-861e-1d875d1b8715",
                                                "text": "Your last delivery of copper ore contained half a hundredweight of tramp metal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0a7669f-a61f-3d05-8e60-af80c61d783e",
                                        "entry_id": "90bb58cd-46f3-3c13-af24-46162a335731",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A metal plate worn by diggers under the hollow of the foot to save the shoe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1159104-6b67-3d77-9ba4-7180ae498fbf",
                                        "entry_id": "90bb58cd-46f3-3c13-af24-46162a335731",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Shaking or juddering of a vehicle's driving axle under hard acceleration or braking, caused by the suspension not fully restraining it, and leading to reduction in tire traction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tramp",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "621cb157-80d7-3f7c-9943-189da68a0b67",
